<span class="ltx_bibblock"><a href="https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2024.naacl-tutorials.3" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">Explanation in the era of large language models</a>.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">In <em id="bib.bib39.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proceedings of the 2024 Conference of the North American Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Human Language Technologies (Volume 5: Tutorial Abstracts)</em>, pages 19–25, Mexico City, Mexico. Association for Computational Linguistics.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs of Theorems</h2>

<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that the calibration set <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{\text{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">cal</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{\text{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the test data are exchangeable. For any desired <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{n}(\lambda)=(\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{1};\mathcal{M}),E_{1}^{*},\lambda)+\ldots+\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}\allowbreak(Q_{n};\mathcal{M}),E_{n}^{*},\lambda))/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{n}(\lambda)=(\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{1};\mathcal{M}),E_{1}^{*},\lambda)+\ldots+\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}\allowbreak(Q_{n};\mathcal{M}),E_{n}^{*},\lambda))/n</annotation></semantics></math> and choose <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> according to Eq. (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2 Methodology ‣ Quantifying Uncertainty in Natural Language Explanations of Large Language Models for Question Answering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). Then, for the constructed uncertainty set <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1}^{*},\hat{\lambda})]\leq\alpha." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1}^{*},\hat{\lambda})]\leq\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider a sequence of exchangeable random loss functions, <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M}),E_{i},\lambda)\}_{i=1}^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M}),E_{i},\lambda)\}_{i=1}^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\cdot,\cdot,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\cdot,\cdot,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> defined in Eq. (<a href="#S2.Ex2" title="In 2 Methodology ‣ Quantifying Uncertainty in Natural Language Explanations of Large Language Models for Question Answering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) is non-increasing in <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, right-continuous, and satisfying <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda_{\max}}(Q_{1};\mathcal{M}),\cdot,\lambda_{\max})\leq\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda_{\max}}(Q_{1};\mathcal{M}),\cdot,\lambda_{\max})\leq\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. We define</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{R}_{n+1}(\lambda)=(\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{1};\mathcal{M}),E_{1},\lambda)+\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{R}_{n+1}(\lambda)=(\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{1};\mathcal{M}),E_{1},\lambda)+\ldots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\lambda))/(n+1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\lambda))/(n+1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}=\inf\{\lambda\in\Lambda:\hat{R}_{n+1}(\lambda)\leq\alpha\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}=\inf\{\lambda\in\Lambda:\hat{R}_{n+1}(\lambda)\leq\alpha\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{\lambda}\ell=\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda_{\max}}(Q_{1};\mathcal{M}),\cdot,\lambda_{\max})\leq\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mi>λ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{\lambda}\ell=\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda_{\max}}(Q_{1};\mathcal{M}),\cdot,\lambda_{\max})\leq\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined almost surely. Since <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\lambda)\leq\sup_{\lambda}\ell=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>λ</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\lambda)\leq\sup_{\lambda}\ell=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{R}_{n+1}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{R}_{n+1}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{n}{n+1}\hat{R}_{n}(\lambda)+\frac{\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\lambda)}{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{n}{n+1}\hat{R}_{n}(\lambda)+\frac{\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\lambda)}{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{n}{n+1}\hat{R}_{n}(\lambda)+\frac{1}{n+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{n}{n+1}\hat{R}_{n}(\lambda)+\frac{1}{n+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we can have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{n}{n+1}\hat{R}_{n}(\lambda)+\frac{1}{n+1}\leq\alpha\Rightarrow\hat{R}_{n+1}(\lambda)\leq\alpha." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{n}{n+1}\hat{R}_{n}(\lambda)+\frac{1}{n+1}\leq\alpha\Rightarrow\hat{R}_{n+1}(\lambda)\leq\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">This implies <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}\leq\hat{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}\leq\hat{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> when the LHS holds for some <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. When the LHS is above <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, by definition, <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\lambda}=\lambda_{\max}\geq\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\lambda}=\lambda_{\max}\geq\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="A1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}\leq\hat{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}\leq\hat{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely. Since <math id="A1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\cdot,\cdot,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\cdot,\cdot,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is non-increasing in <math id="A1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\hat{\lambda})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\hat{\lambda})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\hat{\lambda}^{\prime})]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\hat{\lambda}^{\prime})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> be the multiset of loss functions <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M}),E_{i},\lambda)\}_{i=1}^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M}),E_{i},\lambda)\}_{i=1}^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of <math id="A1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, or equivalently, <math id="A1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant conditional on <math id="A1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, <math id="A1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\lambda)|\mathcal{E}\sim\text{Uniform}(\{\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M}),E_{i},\lambda)\}_{i=1}^{n+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Uniform</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\lambda)|\mathcal{E}\sim\text{Uniform}(\{\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M}),E_{i},\lambda)\}_{i=1}^{n+1})</annotation></semantics></math> by exchangeability. These facts combined with the right-continuity of <math id="A1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> imply</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\hat{\lambda}^{\prime})\mid\mathcal{E}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}^{\prime}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\hat{\lambda}^{\prime})\mid\mathcal{E}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n+1}\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}L_{i}(\hat{\lambda}^{\prime})\leq\alpha." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n+1}\sum_{i=1}^{n+1}L_{i}(\hat{\lambda}^{\prime})\leq\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is completed by the law of total expectation and Eq. (<a href="#A1.Ex11" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems ‣ Quantifying Uncertainty in Natural Language Explanations of Large Language Models for Question Answering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> ULXQA</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          A language model <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, importance score <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}(P_{i},q_{i,j};\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}(P_{i},q_{i,j};\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, calibration data <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{\text{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>cal</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{\text{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math>, test sample <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, Candidate threshold grid <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Lambda=\{\lambda_{1}&lt;\lambda_{2}&lt;\!\dots&lt;\lambda_{K}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.108em">&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda=\{\lambda_{1}&lt;\lambda_{2}&lt;\!\dots&lt;\lambda_{K}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, desired risk level <math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          Uncertainty set <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
             Construct <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M})=\{q_{i,j}\in Q_{i}:\mathcal{S}(P_{i},q_{i,j};\mathcal{M})\geq 1-\lambda\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M})=\{q_{i,j}\in Q_{i}:\mathcal{S}(P_{i},q_{i,j};\mathcal{M})\geq 1-\lambda\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
             Compute <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M}),E_{i}^{*},\lambda_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M}),E_{i}^{*},\lambda_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="low\leftarrow 1,\;high\leftarrow K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">low\leftarrow 1,\;high\leftarrow K</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="low&lt;high" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">low&lt;high</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mid\leftarrow\bigl\lfloor\tfrac{low+high}{2}\bigr\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mid\leftarrow\bigl\lfloor\tfrac{low+high}{2}\bigr\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\smash{\widehat{R}_{n}(\lambda_{mid})\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M}),E_{i}^{*},\lambda_{mid})}{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\smash{\widehat{R}_{n}(\lambda_{mid})\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M}),E_{i}^{*},\lambda_{mid})}{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{n}(\lambda_{mid})\leq\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{n}(\lambda_{mid})\leq\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="high\leftarrow mid" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">high\leftarrow mid</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="low\leftarrow mid+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">low\leftarrow mid+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\lambda}\leftarrow\lambda_{low}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\lambda}\leftarrow\lambda_{low}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
            
            
          Construct the uncertainty set <math id="alg1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M})=\{q_{n+1,j}\in Q_{n+1}:\mathcal{S}(P_{n+1},q_{n+1,j};\mathcal{M})\geq 1-\hat{\lambda}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M})=\{q_{n+1,j}\in Q_{n+1}:\mathcal{S}(P_{n+1},q_{n+1,j};\mathcal{M})\geq 1-\hat{\lambda}\}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfies Eq. (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In Theorem 1. ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Quantifying Uncertainty in Natural Language Explanations of Large Language Models for Question Answering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\prime}_{n+1}\in\mathcal{B}_{Q^{*}_{n+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\prime}_{n+1}\in\mathcal{B}_{Q^{*}_{n+1}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a noisy test question near the clean test question <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{*}_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{*}_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Q^{\prime}_{n+1}-Q^{*}_{n+1}\|_{0}\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Q^{\prime}_{n+1}-Q^{*}_{n+1}\|_{0}\leq d</annotation></semantics></math>. For the above constructed uncertainty set <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}^{\mathcal{R}}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{\prime}_{n+1};\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}^{\mathcal{R}}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{\prime}_{n+1};\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, it satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\ell(\mathcal{C}^{\mathcal{R}}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{\prime}_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1}^{*},\hat{\lambda})]\leq\alpha." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\ell(\mathcal{C}^{\mathcal{R}}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{\prime}_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1}^{*},\hat{\lambda})]\leq\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to the definition of robust score in Eq. (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2 Methodology ‣ Quantifying Uncertainty in Natural Language Explanations of Large Language Models for Question Answering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{R}(P_{n+1},q^{*}_{n+1,j};\mathcal{B}_{Q^{\prime}_{n+1}},\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{R}(P_{n+1},q^{*}_{n+1,j};\mathcal{B}_{Q^{\prime}_{n+1}},\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{S}(P_{n+1},q^{*}_{n+1,j};\mathcal{M})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{S}(P_{n+1},q^{*}_{n+1,j};\mathcal{M}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">for any clean token <math id="A1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{*}_{n+1,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{*}_{n+1,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, which means</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q^{*}_{n+1,j}\in\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{*}_{n+1};\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q^{*}_{n+1,j}\in\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{*}_{n+1};\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q^{*}_{n+1,j}\in\mathcal{C}^{\mathcal{R}}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{\prime}_{n+1};\mathcal{M})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q^{*}_{n+1,j}\in\mathcal{C}^{\mathcal{R}}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{\prime}_{n+1};\mathcal{M}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\ell(\mathcal{C}^{\mathcal{R}}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{\prime}_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\hat{\lambda})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\ell(\mathcal{C}^{\mathcal{R}}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{\prime}_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\hat{\lambda})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{*}_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\hat{\lambda})]\leq\alpha," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{*}_{n+1};\mathcal{M}),E_{n+1},\hat{\lambda})]\leq\alpha,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">which directly implies the result stated in Eq. (<a href="#A1.E14" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems ‣ Quantifying Uncertainty in Natural Language Explanations of Large Language Models for Question Answering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> RULX</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          A language model <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, importance score <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}(P_{i},q_{i,j};\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}(P_{i},q_{i,j};\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, calibration data <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}^{\text{cal}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>cal</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}^{\text{cal}}</annotation></semantics></math>, test sample <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, Candidate threshold grid <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Lambda=\{\lambda_{1}&lt;\lambda_{2}&lt;\!\dots&lt;\lambda_{K}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.108em">&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda=\{\lambda_{1}&lt;\lambda_{2}&lt;\!\dots&lt;\lambda_{K}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, desired risk level <math id="alg2.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
          Uncertainty set <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}^{\mathcal{R}}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{\prime}_{n+1};\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}^{\mathcal{R}}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{\prime}_{n+1};\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
             Construct <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M})=\{q_{i,j}\in Q_{i}:\mathcal{S}(P_{i},q_{i,j};\mathcal{M})\geq 1-\lambda\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M})=\{q_{i,j}\in Q_{i}:\mathcal{S}(P_{i},q_{i,j};\mathcal{M})\geq 1-\lambda\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
             Compute <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M}),E_{i}^{*},\lambda_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M}),E_{i}^{*},\lambda_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="low\leftarrow 1,\;high\leftarrow K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">low\leftarrow 1,\;high\leftarrow K</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="low&lt;high" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">low&lt;high</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mid\leftarrow\bigl\lfloor\tfrac{low+high}{2}\bigr\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mid\leftarrow\bigl\lfloor\tfrac{low+high}{2}\bigr\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\smash{\widehat{R}_{n}(\lambda_{mid})\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M}),E_{i}^{*},\lambda_{mid})}{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\smash{\widehat{R}_{n}(\lambda_{mid})\leftarrow\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{\ell(\mathcal{C}_{\lambda}(Q_{i};\mathcal{M}),E_{i}^{*},\lambda_{mid})}{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}_{n}(\lambda_{mid})\leq\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}_{n}(\lambda_{mid})\leq\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="high\leftarrow mid" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">high\leftarrow mid</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
             <math id="alg2.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="low\leftarrow mid+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">low\leftarrow mid+1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg2.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg2.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
            
            
          <math id="alg2.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\lambda}\leftarrow\lambda_{low}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\lambda}\leftarrow\lambda_{low}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
            
            
          Compute the robust importance score <math id="alg2.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(P_{n+1},\tilde{q}_{n+1,j};\mathcal{B}_{Q^{\prime}_{n+1}},\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(P_{n+1},\tilde{q}_{n+1,j};\mathcal{B}_{Q^{\prime}_{n+1}},\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math> based on Eq. (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2 Methodology ‣ Quantifying Uncertainty in Natural Language Explanations of Large Language Models for Question Answering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
            
            
          Construct the robust uncertainty set <math id="alg2.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}^{\mathcal{R}}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{\prime}_{n+1};\mathcal{M})=\{\tilde{q}_{n+1,j}\in\mathcal{B}_{q^{\prime}_{n+1}}:\mathcal{R}(P_{n+1},\tilde{q}_{n+1,j};\mathcal{B}_{Q^{\prime}_{n+1}},\mathcal{M})\geq 1-\hat{\lambda}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}^{\mathcal{R}}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q^{\prime}_{n+1};\mathcal{M})=\{\tilde{q}_{n+1,j}\in\mathcal{B}_{q^{\prime}_{n+1}}:\mathcal{R}(P_{n+1},\tilde{q}_{n+1,j};\mathcal{B}_{Q^{\prime}_{n+1}},\mathcal{M})\geq 1-\hat{\lambda}\}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisifies Eq. (<a href="#S2.E8" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ 2 Methodology ‣ Quantifying Uncertainty in Natural Language Explanations of Large Language Models for Question Answering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>)

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Algorithms</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Algorithm for ULXQA</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems ‣ Quantifying Uncertainty in Natural Language Explanations of Large Language Models for Question Answering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> describes how to construct the uncertainty set <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math> with the valid uncertainty guarantees for the test-time question <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, this set ensures that, on average, it contains at least a <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> fraction of the ground-truth explanation tokens. This yields a provably valid coverage guarantee for the natural language explanations generated by the model.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Algorithm for RULX</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theorems ‣ Quantifying Uncertainty in Natural Language Explanations of Large Language Models for Question Answering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> outlines the construction of the uncertainty set <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\hat{\lambda}}(Q_{n+1};\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>. This method provides a robust coverage guarantee that the expected fraction of ground-truth explanation tokens included in the uncertainty set remains at least <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, even in the presence of input noise. As a result, it offers reliable uncertainty quantification for natural language explanations under possible perturbations.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Datasets</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopt the following datasets:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MedMCQA</span>. Released under the MIT License for research use, this large-scale benchmark provides expert<span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>verified multiple<span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>choice questions spanning cardiology, oncology, pediatrics, neurology, infectious diseases, and other medical specialties. The dataset is publicly available and contains no personally identifiable information. It is entirely in English, which facilitates evaluation of English<span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text">-</span>language medical QA systems. Although questions center on clinical scenarios, demographic attributes of the underlying patient groups are not specified because such information is absent from the source data.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MedExpQA</span>. Distributed under the CC BY<span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>NC 4.0 license for non<span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text">-</span>commercial research, MedExpQA contains 622 clinician<span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text">-</span>authored multiple<span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text">-</span>choice questions, each paired with gold<span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text">-</span>standard explanations written by medical professionals. The corpus covers four languages (English, Spanish, French, and Italian) and supports cross<span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text">-</span>lingual assessment of answer correctness and explanation quality. It is publicly released and free of personally identifiable information. While items focus on clinical reasoning, demographic details of the represented populations are not included due to the nature of the data.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>AI Assistance in Writing</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During manuscript preparation, we employed an AI language assistant like GPT-o3 for copy<span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>editing tasks—namely, correcting grammar, smoothing phrasing, and improving overall readability. The model was not used to generate scientific ideas, analyses, or conclusions, and it played no role in shaping the study’s methodology or results. Its contribution was limited to language polishing, with all substantive content and final editorial decisions made exclusively by the human authors.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
